  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-25T04:38:49.322Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "My understanding of safemode is it is an emergency button for performance and sensitivity issues. Maybe have all mirrors in the scene be disabled, or at least render just black and nothing else, when safe mode is enabled?\n\nI mention rendering as black as there is a possibility that a mirror is used as some gameplay element and allowing the user to see through a mirror against the world creator's intent would be undesired. So having a opaque placeholder instead could mitigate that concern.\n\nMaybe if safe mode is enabled, have the mirrors render some texture, like \"Mirror Disabled by SafeMode\" text with a black background. IDK, just some spitball ideas atm.",
